<h1>{% if lite %}{% trans %}Ambulatory Glucose Profile{% endtrans %}{% else %}{% trans %}Ambulatory Glucose Profile &amp; CR Assessment{% endtrans %}{% endif %}</h1>
<div class="sub">{{ name }} · {{ span }} · {% trans %}{{ days }} days{% endtrans %} · {{ device }} · {% trans %}sensor wear{% endtrans %} {{ wear }}%</div>
<div class="gen">{% trans %}Created with{% endtrans %} {{ tool }}{% if version %} {{ version }}{% endif %} · {{ generated }} · {% trans %}{{ wlab }} window{% endtrans %} ·
  <a href="{{ repo }}">{{ repo | replace('https://', '') }}</a></div>

{% if source == 'nightscout' or source == 'libreview' %}
<div class="note">{% if source == 'libreview' %}{% trans %}Source: LibreView. Glucose and meal courses only — no basal, no CR assessment.{% endtrans %}{% elif lite %}{% trans %}Source: Nightscout. Glucose and meal courses only — no CR assessment. CamAPS Part 2 is off unless you opt in.{% endtrans %}{% else %}{% trans %}Source: Nightscout dump treated as CamAPS (opt-in). Temp basal is the basal trace.{% endtrans %}{% endif %}</div>
{% endif %}
<div class="disclaimer">
  {% trans %}<b>⚠︎ Not a medical device — analysis only.</b> This tool performs a statistical analysis of
  existing CGM/pump data. It does <b>not</b> provide a diagnosis and <b>no</b> treatment recommendation and
  does not replace medical judgement. <b>Never change insulin, CR, or other settings without your
  diabetes care team.</b> All values serve solely as a basis for discussion; <b>no warranty</b> for
  correctness or completeness.{% endtrans %}
</div>



<div class="part"><h2>{% trans %}Part 1 — what the data shows{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="part-sub">{% trans %}Measurements and courses as recorded. No selection, no assessment.{% endtrans %}</div></div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ mean }}</div><div class="l">{% trans unit=unit %}mean glucose {{ unit }}{% endtrans %}</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ gmi }}%</div><div class="l">GMI</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ cv }}%</div><div class="l">{% trans %}CV (target ≤36%){% endtrans %}</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ tir }}%</div><div class="l">Time in Range</div></div>
</div>


<div class="card">
  <h2>Time in Ranges</h2>
  {% for band in tir_bands %}
  <div class="row"><span>{{ band.label | safe }}</span>
    <div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: {{ band.width }}%; background: {{ band.color }}"></div></div>
    <b>{{ band.val }}%</b></div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">
    {% trans lo=bg70, vlo=bg54, hi=bg140, unit=unit %}Targets: TIR ≥70% · TBR&lt;{{ lo }} &lt;4% · TBR&lt;{{ vlo }} &lt;1% · CV ≤36%. TITR({{ lo }}–{{ hi }} {{ unit }}){% endtrans %} {{ titr }}%.</div>
</div>
<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}AGP (percentiles 5/25/50/75/95){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="chart-wrap"><img class="chart-light" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ agp_img }}"><img class="chart-dark" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ agp_img_dark }}"></div></div>

<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}Real postprandial courses per meal (median){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="chart-wrap"><img class="chart-light" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_img }}"><img class="chart-dark" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_img_dark }}"></div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">{{ curve_cap }}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">{% trans %}This absolute median uses <b>all meals</b> in each slot, including contaminated windows — as do the baseline-normalised curves below. The CR table in Part 2 prefers contamination-free meals instead (at least 3 clean, otherwise all), so its count (n) can differ; how much that selection changes the picture is stated there.{% endtrans %}</div></div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Course relative to meal start (baseline-normalised){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="chart-wrap"><img class="chart-light" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_norm_img }}"><img class="chart-dark" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_norm_img_dark }}"></div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">
    {% trans w=wlab %}Each meal is set to <b>0 at minute 0</b>, then the median is taken — the typical
    <b>net course</b>. Its value at the end is the Δ{{ w }} used later. Ending negative → often below baseline
    (overdosing); staying high → underdosing. <b>All meals</b> of a slot are shown here, like the
    absolute curve above: this is what happened, without any selection. n can differ slightly when
    minute 0 has no CGM sample.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

{% if not lite %}
<div class="part"><h2>{% trans %}Part 2 — assessment and how to read it{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="part-sub">{% trans %}Everything from here rests on the method described in this part.{% endtrans %}</div></div>

<div class="methodbox">
  <b>{% trans %}How to read this report (CamAPS FX Auto Mode){% endtrans %}</b><br>
  {% trans %}• <b>Scope:</b> Built for CamAPS FX Auto Mode, where the algorithm mainly corrects via
  <b>modulated basal</b> (not auto-bolus). Other AID systems need a different signal.{% endtrans %}<br>
  {% trans %}• <b>Loop extra basal</b> in the post-meal window:
  <code>∫ (basal rate − fasting basal) dt</code>.
  Positive → extra Auto Mode activity after the meal. It can fit a too-weak CR, but on real CamAPS it is not specific to that.{% endtrans %}<br>
  {% trans %}• <b>Two ratios:</b>
  <code>CR (CHO/bolus)</code> = carbs ÷ meal bolus only (may include correction insulin).
  <code>CR_eff</code> = CHO ÷ (bolus + loop extra basal) — effective ratio <i>including</i> loop compensation.
  Neither is a programmed pump setting; both are derived from the export.
  If the loop already adds or cuts a lot of insulin with no meal, that says nothing about the carb ratios. The less non-meal loop influence in the window, the less CR_eff is shifted by that extra Auto Mode activity.{% endtrans %}<br>
  {% trans %}• <b>Use:</b> Discussion material for the diabetes care team only — not a dosing instruction.{% endtrans %}
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}CR assessment per slot, and what follows from it{% endtrans %}</h2>
  {% if rest %}
  <div class="note" style="margin:0 0 10px; padding:8px 10px; border-left:3px solid var(--method-b); background:var(--method-bg)">
    {% if rest.rel is not none %}
      {% trans pct='%.0f'|format(rest.rel*100) %}Away from meals the basal was typically about {{ pct }} % off the overnight average. That is common under CamAPS — it does not say whether the carb ratio is wrong.{% endtrans %}
    {% else %}
      {% trans %}Too little time without a meal to compare the basal to overnight. The table below is still only discussion material.{% endtrans %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>{% trans %}Slot{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}n (clean){% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Ø CHO{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}CR (CHO/bolus){% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Bolus{% endtrans %}</th>
        <th>{% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ wlab }}</th><th>{% trans %}CR_eff (+loop){% endtrans %}</th><th>Δ{{ wlab }}</th><th>{% trans %}Verdict{% endtrans %}</th></tr>
    {% for s in slots %}
    {% set unstable = s.stability and s.stability.band == 'low' %}
    <tr class="{{ s.cls }}{{ ' lowconf' if s.low_confidence or unstable }}"><td>{{ s.label }}{% if s.low_confidence %} <span class="lc-tag">{% trans %}low confidence{% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}{% if unstable %} <span class="lc-tag">{% trans %}verdict not stable{% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}</td><td>{{ s.n }} ({{ s.clean }})</td>
        <td>{{ s.cho }} g</td><td>{{ s.cr }}</td><td>{{ s.bol }} U</td>
        <td>{{ s.exc }} U</td><td>{{ s.cre }}</td><td>{{ s.d4 }}</td><td>{{ s.flag }}{% if s.stability %}<div class="meta{{ ' low' if s.stability.band == 'low' }}">{% trans pct=s.stability.pct %}Stability {{ pct }}{% endtrans %} % · {{ s.stability.days }} {% trans %}calendar days{% endtrans %}{% if s.stability.few_days %} <span class="fewd">{% trans %}(few){% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}{% if s.spread and s.spread.cre %} · {% trans cre=s.spread.cre %}spread CR_eff {{ cre }}{% endtrans %}{% elif s.range and s.range.cre %} · {% trans cre=s.range.cre %}observed CR_eff {{ cre }}{% endtrans %}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px"><span class="tag ts">{% trans %}too strong → loosen{% endtrans %}</span><span class="tag tw">{% trans %}too weak → tighten{% endtrans %}</span><span class="tag to">{% trans %}plausibly adequate{% endtrans %}</span><br><br></div>
  <div class="note">{% if selection %}
    <b>{% trans %}Selection used for the verdict:{% endtrans %}</b>
    {% for s in selection %}{{ s.label }} {{ s.used }}/{{ s.total }} ({{ s.shift }} {{ unit }}){% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
    {% trans %}The verdict uses only meals without another meal in the window and without a large CGM
    gap. The value in brackets is how far that selection would move the baseline-normalised curves
    shown in Part 1 — a small number means those curves also describe what the verdict rests
    on.{% endtrans %}{% endif %}</div>
  <h3 style="font-size:13px;margin:14px 0 4px">{% trans %}Derivations from the curve shape &amp; possible approaches{% endtrans %}</h3>
  {% for r in recs %}
  {% set unstable = r.stability and r.stability.band == 'low' %}
  <div class="slot {{ r.cls }}{{ ' lowconf' if r.low_confidence or unstable }}">
    <h3>{{ r.label }} — {{ r.headline }}{% if r.low_confidence %} <span class="lc-tag">{% trans %}low confidence{% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}{% if unstable %} <span class="lc-tag">{% trans %}verdict not stable{% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
    <div class="mline">{% trans %}Peak{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.peak }} {{ unit }}</b> {% trans %}after{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.peak_t }} min</b> ·
      {% trans %}nadir{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.nadir }} {{ unit }}</b> @ {{ r.nadir_t }} min · Δ{{ wlab }} <b>{{ r.d4 }}</b> ·
      {% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ r.loop }} U · {% trans %}CR (CHO/bolus){% endtrans %} {{ r.cr }} · CR_eff {{ r.cre }}</div>
    {% if r.spread or r.range or r.stability %}<div class="meta{{ ' low' if r.stability and r.stability.band == 'low' }}">{% if r.spread %}{% trans %}Spread{% endtrans %}{% if r.spread.cre %} CR_eff {{ r.spread.cre }}{% endif %}{% if r.spread.ratio %} · {% trans %}loop{% endtrans %} {{ r.spread.ratio }}{% endif %}{% elif r.range %}{% trans cre=r.range.cre, meals=r.range.meals, days=r.range.days %}Observed CR_eff {{ cre }} ({{ meals }} meals / {{ days }} days){% endtrans %}{% endif %}{% if (r.spread or r.range) and r.stability %} · {% endif %}{% if r.stability %}{% trans pct=r.stability.pct %}stability {{ pct }}{% endtrans %} % ({{ r.stability.days }} {% trans %}calendar days{% endtrans %}){% if r.stability.few_days %} <span class="fewd">{% trans %}(few){% endtrans %}</span>{% endif %}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
    {% for l in r.levers %}
    <div class="lever"><span class="tag t-{{ l.cls }}">{{ l.tag }}</span>{{ l.text }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">{% trans %}Hypotheses/candidates for the team discussion, not a
    dosing instruction. Under Auto Mode the loop co-shapes the curve.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>


<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Explanations &amp; limits{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="note" style="margin: 6px 0 0">
    <b>{% trans %}Time windows:{% endtrans %}</b> {{ slot_defs | join(' · ') }}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin: 6px 0 0">
    <b>{% trans %}Fasting basal rate:{% endtrans %}</b> {{ fb }} U/h{% if fb_lo != fb_hi %} ({% trans lo=fb_lo, hi=fb_hi %}mean of the nights; {{ lo }}–{{ hi }} U/h{% endtrans %}){% endif %} —
    {% trans %}the reference the loop extra basal is measured against. It assumes meal- and correction-free
    nights 00:00–06:00; if that does not hold, every "Loop" figure shifts with it.{% endtrans %}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">
    {% trans w=wlab %}<b>Method:</b> Loop {{ w }} = basal delivered by Auto Mode in addition to the
    fasting basal rate. <b>CR (CHO/bolus)</b> = CHO / meal bolus only (not the pump’s programmed ICR).
    <b>CR_eff (+loop)</b> = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal). Δ{{ w }} = glucose at
    {{ w }} minus pre-meal. "clean" = meals without another meal in the {{ w }} window and without a
    large CGM gap.{% endtrans %}
    {% trans %}<b>⚠︎</b> on the verdict = fewer than 3 clean meals; the statement relies (in part)
    on contaminated windows and is correspondingly less certain.{% endtrans %}
    {% trans %}<b>Hatched row</b> = same low-confidence case (fewer than 3 clean meals); treat the colour class with extra caution.{% endtrans %}
    <br>
    {% trans %}<b>Stability:</b> shown next to a verdict where enough meals on enough separate
    days exist. It resamples whole recorded days with replacement and re-runs the same rule:{% endtrans %}
    90 % = {% trans %}robust{% endtrans %}; 40 % = {% trans %}a few days flip it{% endtrans %}.
    {% trans %}It states how sensitive the verdict is to <b>which meals happened to be recorded</b> —
    not how likely the carb ratio is correct, and not a confidence interval for a true value. A verdict
    that flips under resampling rests on a few individual meals; one that holds does not become
    clinically right by that alone. The thresholds for high/moderate/low are heuristic.{% endtrans %}
    <br>
    {% trans %}<b>Spread:</b> typical{% endtrans %} 95 % {% trans %}band of CR_eff (and loop share) when days are reshuffled (enough days only).{% endtrans %}
    <br>
    {% trans %}<b>Observed range:</b> min–max of the actual values when there are too few days for a spread.{% endtrans %}
    {% trans %}Neither is a confidence interval for “the true CR”.{% endtrans %}
    <br>
    {% trans lo=15, hi=25, few=34, many=3 %}<b>How much does it take?</b> Measured on synthetic data: a carb-ratio error below about {{ lo }} % stays invisible to this method, from about {{ hi }} % it is flagged reliably. Days matter mostly against false alarms — with five days a correctly set slot is still flagged in roughly {{ few }} % of cases, with three weeks in about {{ many }} %. A day count marked {% endtrans %}<b>{% trans %}(few){% endtrans %}</b>{% trans n=10 %} is below {{ n }} days, where that risk is still noticeable.{% endtrans %}</div>
  <div class="eff">
    {% trans %}<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal the loop pushed in
    into an "effectively used" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal)</code>.{% endtrans %}
    {% if cr_example %}<br><br>{% trans label=cr_example.label, cho=cr_example.cho, bol=cr_example.bol, loop=cr_example.loop, cre=cr_example.cre %}Example {{ label }}: {{ cho }} g on
    ({{ bol }} U bolus + {{ loop }} U loop) ≈ <b>{{ cre }}</b>
    instead of the configured ratio.{% endtrans %}{% if cr_example.underdosed %} {% trans w=wlab, d4=cr_example.d4, unit=unit %}And even then the BG at
    {{ w }} is still <b>{{ d4 }} {{ unit }}</b> above baseline — the loop-boosted amount
    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound here</b>: the actually needed CR
    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units).{% endtrans %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
    <br><br>{% trans %}<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude — <b>not</b> an exact pump setting.
    Approximation (loop extra fully attributed to the meal; corrections/exercise/adaptation possible).
    Small step with the team; re-check after ~1–2 weeks.{% endtrans %}</div>
  <div class="note">
    {% trans %}This is <b>decision evidence for the diabetes care team</b>, not a dosing instruction.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {{ cr_note | safe }}
    {% trans %}• Under CamAPS Auto Mode the loop compensates continuously; that is exactly why the loop extra
      basal is the meaningful signal. The algorithm adapts over days and can partly smooth out
      longer-standing misconfigurations.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {% trans %}• Confounders (fat/protein, exercise, split boluses, overlapping meals) are dampened by medians,
      not eliminated; slots with few "clean" meals{% endtrans %}{{ clean_note }} {% trans %}are less certain.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {% trans %}• <b>Boost / Ease-off</b> are not present in the Glooko CSV export and cannot be detected automatically.
      If either mode is active somewhere in the post-meal window, loop extra basal and CR signals can be
      distorted — interpret such windows with the care team; exclude them mentally from CR conclusions if known.{% endtrans %}<br><br>
  </div>
</div>


{% endif %}
{% if meals %}
<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Per-meal detail{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>{% trans %}Time{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Slot{% endtrans %}</th><th>CHO g</th><th>Bolus U</th><th>{% trans %}CR (CHO/bolus){% endtrans %}</th>
        {% if not lite %}<th>{% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ wlab }} U</th><th>{% trans %}CR_eff (+loop){% endtrans %}</th>{% endif %}<th>Δ{{ wlab }}</th><th>⚠︎</th></tr>
    {% for m in meals %}
    <tr><td>{{ m.time }}</td><td>{{ m.label }}</td><td>{{ m.cho }}</td>
        <td>{{ m.bolus }}</td><td>{{ m.cr }}</td>{% if not lite %}<td>{{ m.exc }}</td><td>{{ m.cre }}</td>{% endif %}
        <td>{% if m.low_d4 %}<b class="d4low">{{ m.d4 }}</b>{% else %}{{ m.d4 }}{% endif %}</td><td>{% if m.hypo_rescue %}<span title="{% trans %}hypo rescue in the window{% endtrans %}">⚠︎ H</span>{% elif m.contam %}<span title="{% trans %}contaminated window{% endtrans %}">⚠︎</span>{% elif m.cgm_gap %}<span title="{% trans %}CGM gap in the window{% endtrans %}">⚠︎ G</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">{% trans w=wlab %}⚠︎ = contaminated window (another meal &lt;{{ w }} afterwards). ⚠︎ H = a hypo rescue (small carbs, no bolus, low BG) in the window. ⚠︎ G = CGM gap over 25 min in the window (excluded from the clean median when enough other meals exist).{% endtrans %}
    {% trans lo=-30 %}A Δ4h below {{ lo }} is set in colour: that meal ended well below its
    starting value. Rows are deliberately not colour-coded — a single meal carries far too
    little signal to be judged on its own.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% if daily_days %}
<div class="part"><h2>{% trans %}Appendix — daily courses{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="part-sub">{% trans %}Raw daily plots, unfiltered.{% endtrans %}</div></div>

<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}Daily overview — CGM · bolus · basal{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="note">{% trans lo=tir_lo, hi=tir_hi, unit=unit %}Green band = target range {{ lo }}–{{ hi }} {{ unit }} · <b style="color:#0b2e6b">units</b>
    = bolus · <span style="color:#c0392b">grams</span> = carbs (all individual entries) ·
    blue area below = basal rate (U/h scale on the right, same for all days). One panel per day.{% endtrans %}</div></div>
{% for d in daily_days %}
<div class="dailyrow chart-wrap"><img class="chart-light" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ d.img }}">{% if d.img_dark %}<img class="chart-dark" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ d.img_dark }}">{% endif %}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

</div>
</body>
</html>
